CLASS Core
    DESCRIPTION: Handles core API communication, encryption, and app state management
    NAMESPACE: NewgroundsIO
    
    PURPOSE: This class is the heart of the Newgrounds.io library. It handles:
    - Network communication with the Newgrounds servers
    - Encrypting secure components to prevent cheating
    - Managing a queue of components to send in batch requests
    - Parsing server responses and updating the app state
    
    WHY SEPARATE?: Developers should use the NGIO wrapper for simple tasks, but advanced users
    can access Core directly for more control (via NGIO.core).
    
    ====================
    CONSTANTS
    ====================
    
    GATEWAY_URL = "https://www.newgrounds.io/gateway_v3.php"
        PURPOSE: The server endpoint where all API calls are sent.
        WHY: All requests go to this single URL on the Newgrounds servers.

    LIBRARY_VERSION = "1.0.0"
        PURPOSE: The version of THIS library - your port, not the gateway and not the app.
        WHY: Several Newgrounds.io libraries exist, of differing vintage. When someone
        reports a bug against "the Newgrounds.io library", this is what identifies which
        one and which revision they actually have. Bump it when you release a change, and
        log it at init alongside the app id and build version.

    MAX_QUEUE_SIZE = 10
        PURPOSE: Maximum number of components that can be bundled in a single request.
        WHY: The server has limits to prevent abuse. If we send too many at once, the server rejects it.

    UNKNOWN_STATUS = 0
        PURPOSE: Stands in for "the platform reported no HTTP status".
        WHY: 0 is not a real status, so it cannot collide with one. Treat it as UNKNOWN,
        never as an error in itself - and never substitute a plausible-looking status
        such as 500 for it. See onHTTPResponse for why that distinction matters to the
        message a player ends up reading.

    ====================
    READONLY PROPERTIES
    ====================
    
    appId: string
        PURPOSE: Stores the app ID provided at initialization.
        WHY: Every request needs the app ID so the server knows which app is making the request.
    
    buildVersion: string | null
        PURPOSE: Stores the app's version number provided at initialization.
        WHY: Used to check if the app is outdated and notify the user to update.
    
    appState: NewgroundsIO.AppState
        PURPOSE: Stores cached data loaded from the server (medals, scoreboards, etc.)
        WHY: Instead of contacting the server repeatedly, we cache the data locally for fast access.
    
    ====================
    PUBLIC PROPERTIES
    ====================
    
    debugNetworkCalls: boolean = false
        PURPOSE: Set to true to show packets going to and from the server.
        WHY: Helps debug network issues by logging all request/response data.
        USAGE: Set to true during development to see what's being sent to the server.
    
    networkObserver: function|null = null
        PURPOSE: Optional callback receiving raw gateway traffic, as
        function(direction: string, detail: string).
        WHY: debugNetworkCalls only writes to the console, which cannot be captured.
        An observer hands the same packets to the host application, so they can be
        attached to a log entry, shown in-game, or held against a failing test.
        USAGE: Independent of debugNetworkCalls - either, both or neither may be set.
        'direction' is one of "request", "response" or "error".
    
    useDebugMode: boolean = false
        PURPOSE: If true, API calls don't actually save to the server.
        WHY: Useful for testing - you can unlock medals, post scores, etc. without affecting
        the actual game data. When a developer tests, they don't want test data in the real system.
    
    ====================
    PRIVATE PROPERTIES
    ====================
    
    encryptionKeyBytes: BinaryData
        PURPOSE: Stores the encryption key used to encrypt secure components (decoded from Base64).
        WHY: The library encrypts certain components (like medal unlocks) to prevent cheating.
        NOTE: Implementation varies by platform. See IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE.txt for encryption patterns.
        SECURITY: Store as binary/bytes for better performance and security.
    
    componentQueue: array = []
        PURPOSE: Temporary storage for components waiting to be sent to the server.
        WHY: Instead of sending each component immediately, we batch them together for efficiency.
        This means one network request can execute multiple components at once.
    
    ====================
    CONSTRUCTOR
    ====================
    
    CONSTRUCTOR(appId: string, encryptionKey: string, buildVersion: string|null = null, useDebugMode: boolean = false)
        
        PURPOSE: Initialize the Core object with the settings needed to communicate with the server.
        
        PARAMETERS:
            appId: (required) The unique identifier for the app (from Newgrounds)
            encryptionKey: (required) The Base64-encoded key used for encryption (from Newgrounds)
            buildVersion: (optional, default: null) The app's version number in XX.XX.XXXX format
            useDebugMode: (optional, default: false) Whether to run in test mode (components execute but don't save to server)
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Store all the configuration values we'll need
            SET this.appId TO appId
            
            COMMENT: Decode Base64 encryption key once and store as bytes
            IF encryptionKey is null OR encryptionKey.length equals 0 THEN
                LOG_ERROR("Encryption Error: Missing Base64 encryption key")
                SET this.encryptionKeyBytes TO empty byte array
            ELSE
                TRY
                    SET this.encryptionKeyBytes TO DECODE_BASE64(encryptionKey)
                CATCH error
                    LOG_ERROR("Encryption Error: Invalid Base64 encryption key - " + error)
                    SET this.encryptionKeyBytes TO empty byte array
                END TRY
            END IF
            
            SET this.buildVersion TO buildVersion
            SET this.useDebugMode TO useDebugMode
            
            COMMENT: Create an empty queue for components
            COMMENT: This will be filled by queueComponent() and sent by executeQueue()
            SET this.componentQueue TO []
            
            COMMENT: Create a new AppState instance
            SET this.appState TO new NewgroundsIO.AppState(this)
            
    END CONSTRUCTOR
    
    ====================
    PUBLIC METHODS
    ====================
    
    FUNCTION hasSession(): boolean
        
        PURPOSE: Check if the user has an active session.
        WHY: Many operations require a logged-in user with a valid session.
        
        RETURNS: true if there's an active session with a valid session ID
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            RETURN (appState is not null AND 
                    appState.session is not null AND 
                    appState.session.id is not null AND 
                    appState.session.id.length > 0)
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION GET sessionId(): string | null
        
        PURPOSE: Get the current session ID.
        WHY: Convenient access to session ID for checking login state.
        
        RETURNS: The current session ID, or null if no session exists
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            IF appState is not null AND appState.session is not null THEN
                RETURN appState.session.id
            END IF
            RETURN null
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION SET sessionId(value: string)
        
        PURPOSE: Set the session ID.
        WHY: Allows manually setting session after login or restoration from storage.
        
        PARAMETERS:
            value: (required) The session ID to set
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            IF appState is not null THEN
                IF appState.session is null THEN
                    COMMENT: Create a new session if needed
                    SET appState.session TO ObjectFactory.CreateObject("Session", null, this)
                END IF
                SET appState.session.id TO value
            END IF
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION callComponent(componentPath: string, componentParams: object|null = null, callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null, callbackParams: object|null = null)
        
        PURPOSE: Convenience method to call a component directly with parameters.
        WHY: This handles creating the component, executing it, and managing callbacks in one call.
        
        PARAMETERS:
            componentPath: (required) The component to call (e.g. "Medal.unlock")
            componentParams: (optional) Parameters for the component
            callback: (optional) Function to call with the response
            thisArg: (optional) Context for the callback
            callbackParams: (optional) Caller data passed through to callback as second argument
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            response: (Required) Response model on success, or local error object on local failure
            callbackParams: (optional) Caller data passed through unchanged
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Parse the component path (e.g. "Medal.unlock" -> component="Medal", method="unlock")
            CREATE parts AS SPLIT(componentPath, ".")
            IF parts.length NOT equals 2 THEN
                LOG_ERROR("callComponent Error: Invalid component path - " + componentPath)
                IF callback is not null THEN
                    CREATE error AS {success: false, error: "Invalid component path: " + componentPath}
                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING error, callbackParams
                END IF
                RETURN
            END IF
            
            CREATE componentName AS parts[0]
            CREATE methodName AS parts[1]
            
            TRY
                COMMENT: Create component using ObjectFactory if available
                CREATE component AS ObjectFactory.CreateComponent(componentName, methodName, null, this)

                IF component is null THEN
                    IF callback is not null THEN
                        CREATE errorResult AS {success: false, error: "Component not found: " + componentPath}
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING errorResult, callbackParams
                    END IF
                    RETURN
                END IF
                
                IF component is not null AND componentParams is not null THEN
                    COMMENT: Prefer model import for casting/validation; fall back to direct copy.
                    IF component supports importFromObject THEN
                        CALL component.importFromObject(componentParams)
                    ELSE
                        FOR EACH key IN componentParams
                            IF component has property key THEN
                                SET component[key] TO componentParams[key]
                            END IF
                        END FOR
                    END IF
                END IF
                
                COMMENT: Execute the component
                IF callback is not null THEN
                    CALL executeComponent(component, FUNCTION(response)
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING response, callbackParams
                    END FUNCTION)
                ELSE
                    CALL executeComponent(component, null)
                END IF
            CATCH error
                LOG_ERROR("callComponent Error: " + error)
                COMMENT: Component not found or error creating it
                IF callback is not null THEN
                    CREATE errorResult AS {success: false, error: "Component not found: " + componentPath}
                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING errorResult, callbackParams
                END IF
            END TRY
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION queueComponent(componentModel: NewgroundsIO.BaseComponent)
        
        PURPOSE: Add a component to the queue of components to send.
        WHY: Queuing lets us send multiple components in one network request for efficiency.
        
        PARAMETERS:
            componentModel: A component instance (like Medal.unlock) ready to send
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Check that the queue isn't full
            COMMENT: If it is, sending it would exceed the server's limits
            IF componentQueue.length < MAX_QUEUE_SIZE THEN
                COMMENT: Wrap the component in an Execute object for transmission
                CREATE executeModel AS ObjectFactory.CreateObject("Execute", null, this)
                
                CALL executeModel.setComponent(componentModel)
                
                COMMENT: Add to queue
                APPEND executeModel TO componentQueue
            ELSE
                COMMENT: Queue is full - this is a developer error
                THROW error "Component queue limit exceeded"
            END IF
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION executeQueue(callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)
        
        PURPOSE: Send all queued components to the server in a single request.
        WHY: Batching requests improves performance and reduces server load.
        Note: Components are already wrapped in Execute objects by queueComponent()
        
        PARAMETERS:
            callback: Function called with (resultModel) when server replies
            thisArg: Context for the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            resultModel: (Required) NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Response - The response object returned from the server
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: If queue is empty, nothing to do
            IF componentQueue.length equals 0 THEN
                IF callback is not null THEN
                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING null
                END IF
                RETURN
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: ==================== STEP 1: PARTITION ====================
            COMMENT: Sort the queue into redirects and batchable wrappers. Do NOT send
            COMMENT: anything yet, and do NOT clear the queue yet. Partition, then clear,
            COMMENT: then act - dispatching network work while still walking a queue you
            COMMENT: are about to clear is how this method breaks.
            CREATE redirectComponents AS new array
            CREATE toExecute AS new array
            CREATE refusedComponents AS new array

            FOR EACH executeWrapper IN componentQueue
                COMMENT: Get the component model inside the Execute wrapper
                CREATE componentModel AS executeWrapper.componentModel

                COMMENT: Check if the wrapped component is a redirect loader
                COMMENT: These open external windows instead of returning JSON responses
                COMMENT: The flag is named `redirect` on BaseComponent, so every component
                COMMENT: carries it. Test its value, not its presence - presence checks are
                COMMENT: unreliable across platforms (see the hasOwnProperty note in
                COMMENT: BaseObject.pseudo) and there is nothing to detect here anyway.
                CREATE isRedirect AS false
                IF componentModel is not null AND componentModel.redirect equals true THEN
                    SET isRedirect TO true
                END IF

                IF isRedirect equals true THEN
                    APPEND componentModel TO redirectComponents
                    CONTINUE TO NEXT COMPONENT
                END IF

                COMMENT: Refuse what cannot succeed, but KEEP IT IN THE REPORT.
                COMMENT: The caller asked for this component and is owed an answer
                COMMENT: about it, in the same shape the server would have used.
                COMMENT:
                COMMENT: A batch is partial by nature - the gateway refuses
                COMMENT: individual components while running their siblings, which
                COMMENT: is why loadData can ask for medals and saveSlots together
                COMMENT: and get one of them. Refusing the WHOLE batch because one
                COMMENT: component lacks a session would lose the medals a
                COMMENT: signed-out title screen legitimately wanted.
                IF componentModel is not null THEN
                    CREATE preflightError AS CALL componentModel.getPreflightError()

                    IF preflightError is not null THEN
                        APPEND {component: componentModel, error: preflightError} TO refusedComponents
                        CONTINUE TO NEXT COMPONENT
                    END IF
                END IF

                COMMENT: Add the already-wrapped Execute object to the batch
                COMMENT: It's already been processed by queueComponent() and has the component set
                SET executeWrapper.core TO this
                APPEND executeWrapper TO toExecute
            END FOR

            COMMENT: ==================== STEP 2: CLEAR ====================
            COMMENT: Queue has been processed - clear it for next batch
            CLEAR componentQueue

            COMMENT: ==================== STEP 3: ACT ====================
            COMMENT: Send each redirect on its own, WITHOUT the caller's callback.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: This is the part that is easy to get wrong. The callback is in scope
            COMMENT: and passing it looks helpful, but a redirect exchanges no JSON - it
            COMMENT: fires its callback with null. Pass the caller's callback here and a
            COMMENT: queue holding one redirect plus one normal component invokes that
            COMMENT: callback TWICE: once with null from the redirect, then once with the
            COMMENT: real Response from the batch.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: Callers cannot defend against that, because the empty-queue case above
            COMMENT: legitimately calls back with null too - so a careful caller reads the
            COMMENT: first invocation as "nothing to do" and discards the real response.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: executeQueue invokes the caller's callback EXACTLY ONCE, with either
            COMMENT: null or a Response. The redirects are fire-and-forget.
            FOR EACH redirectComponent IN redirectComponents
                CALL executeComponent(redirectComponent)
            END FOR

            COMMENT: If we ended up with no components to send, we're done
            IF toExecute.length equals 0 THEN
                COMMENT: ...unless everything was refused locally, in which case
                COMMENT: the caller is owed a report saying so. Answering null here
                COMMENT: would mean "nothing to do", which is the one thing that
                COMMENT: did not happen.
                IF refusedComponents.length > 0 THEN
                    IF callback is not null THEN
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                            PASSING buildRefusalResponseList(refusedComponents)
                    END IF
                    RETURN
                END IF

                IF callback is not null THEN
                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING null
                END IF
                RETURN
            END IF

            COMMENT: Some were refused but others are going out. Send the valid
            COMMENT: ones, then fold the refusals into the response so the caller
            COMMENT: gets ONE report covering everything it queued - which is how
            COMMENT: the gateway would have answered had it done the refusing.
            IF refusedComponents.length > 0 THEN
                CALL sendRequest(toExecute, false,
                    FUNCTION onComplete(response)
                        IF callback is not null THEN
                            CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                                PASSING mergeRefusalsIntoResponse(response, refusedComponents)
                        END IF
                    END FUNCTION,
                    null)
                RETURN
            END IF

            COMMENT: Send all the components to the server
            CALL sendRequest(toExecute, false, callback, thisArg)
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION executeComponent(componentModel: NewgroundsIO.BaseComponent, callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)
        
        PURPOSE: Execute a single component immediately (not queued).
        WHY: Some components need immediate execution, not batching.
        
        PARAMETERS:
            componentModel: The component to execute
            callback: Function called with (resultModel) when server replies
            thisArg: Context for the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            resultModel: (Required) NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Response - The response object returned from the server
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Set core reference on component if not already set
            IF componentModel is not null AND componentModel.core is null THEN
                SET componentModel.core TO this
            END IF

            COMMENT: ==================== PREFLIGHT ====================
            COMMENT: Refuse a component that cannot possibly succeed, WITHOUT
            COMMENT: spending a request on it. See getPreflightError() in
            COMMENT: BaseComponent.pseudo for what is and is not decidable here.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN "SAVING A REQUEST": the gateway
            COMMENT: limits requests per time window. A game calling
            COMMENT: medal.unlock() on every scoring event while the player has no
            COMMENT: session spends that budget on calls whose outcome was
            COMMENT: knowable before they left the machine - and then a call that
            COMMENT: COULD have succeeded gets a 429.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: THE CONTRACT, and the rule that makes this safe to add:
            COMMENT: DO NOT INVENT A NEW FAILURE SHAPE. A locally-refused call
            COMMENT: must be indistinguishable from a server-refused one except by
            COMMENT: how fast it arrives - same Response shape, same result shape,
            COMMENT: same error codes. Then nothing downstream needs a special
            COMMENT: case, and the three-layer check in AppState.loadData and the
            COMMENT: NGIO wrappers reads a synthesized refusal exactly as it reads
            COMMENT: a real one. A local error that arrived differently would mean
            COMMENT: every caller needs two code paths for one condition.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: REDIRECTS ARE EXEMPT: they navigate the browser rather than
            COMMENT: exchanging JSON, so there is no response to shape - and the
            COMMENT: one that matters (App.startSession -> Passport) is how a
            COMMENT: session gets established in the first place.
            CREATE isRedirect AS componentModel.redirect

            IF isRedirect is not true THEN
                CREATE preflightError AS CALL componentModel.getPreflightError()

                IF preflightError is not null THEN
                    CALL reportNetworkActivity("error", "Refused before sending - " + preflightError.message)

                    IF callback is not null THEN
                        CALL callback WITH context thisArg
                            PASSING buildRefusalResponse(componentModel, preflightError)
                    END IF
                    RETURN
                END IF
            END IF

            COMMENT: Wrap the component for transmission
            CREATE executeModel AS ObjectFactory.CreateObject("Execute", null, this)
            
            SET executeModel.core TO this
            CALL executeModel.setComponent(componentModel)
            
            COMMENT: Get redirect flag from the component
            CREATE isRedirect AS componentModel.redirect
            COMMENT: Send it with the redirect flag from the component
            CALL sendRequest(executeModel, isRedirect, callback, thisArg)
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION encryptObject(obj: object): string | null
        
        PURPOSE: Encrypts a plain object to obfuscate secure components.
        WHY: Makes cheating harder - medal unlocks and score posts are encrypted.
        
        PARAMETERS:
            obj: The plain object to encrypt (usually a JSON-compatible object)
        
        RETURNS: The encrypted data encoded as Base64 string, or null if encryption failed
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            TRY
                COMMENT: Convert the object to a JSON string
                CREATE jsonString AS JSON_ENCODE(obj)
            CATCH error
                LOG_ERROR("Encryption Error: Failed to convert object to JSON - " + error)
                RETURN null
            END TRY

            TRY
                COMMENT: Encrypt the JSON string using the encryption key
                CREATE encryptedString AS CALL encryptData(jsonString)
            CATCH error
                LOG_ERROR("Encryption Error: Failed to encrypt JSON string - " + error)
                RETURN null
            END TRY

            RETURN encryptedString
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION encryptData(text: string): string | null
        
        PURPOSE: Encrypts text (usually JSON) to obfuscate secure components.
        WHY: Makes cheating harder - medal unlocks and score posts are encrypted so cheaters can't easily manipulate server requests.
        
        IMPLEMENTATION: Uses AES-128-CBC (Advanced Encryption Standard, 128-bit key, Cipher Block Chaining mode)
        - Padding: PKCS5 (standard padding for block ciphers)
        - Output: Base64-encoded ciphertext with prepended IV
        
        PARAMETERS:
            text: The data to encrypt (usually a JSON string)
        
        RETURNS: The encrypted data encoded as Base64 string, or null if encryption failed
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Use the cached Base64-decoded encryption key bytes
            IF this.encryptionKeyBytes is null OR this.encryptionKeyBytes.length equals 0 THEN
                LOG_ERROR("Encryption Error: Encryption key bytes not set")
                RETURN null
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Create a copy of the key bytes for encryption
            CREATE keyBytes AS COPY(this.encryptionKeyBytes)
            
            COMMENT: Create AES-128-CBC cipher with automatic IV handling
            COMMENT: See IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE.txt for platform-specific encryption patterns
            CREATE cipher AS CREATE_CIPHER("AES-128-CBC", keyBytes, "PKCS5")
            
            COMMENT: Convert the input text to binary data
            CREATE inputBytes AS TEXT_TO_BYTES(text)
            
            COMMENT: Encrypt the data
            COMMENT: The cipher modifies the binary data in-place
            CALL cipher.encrypt(inputBytes)
            
            COMMENT: Encode encrypted bytes as Base64 string for transmission
            CREATE encryptedBase64 AS ENCODE_BASE64(inputBytes)
            
            RETURN encryptedBase64
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION reportNetworkActivity(direction: string, detail: string)

        PURPOSE: Hand a raw gateway packet to networkObserver, if one is attached.
        WHY: debugNetworkCalls can only write to a console. Games and test harnesses
        need the same packets as data - to attach to a bug report, surface in a
        debug overlay, or hold against a failing test. This is the one place that
        decision is made, so every transport path reports identically.

        PARAMETERS:
            direction: "request", "response" or "error"
            detail: The raw payload, or a description of the error

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF this.networkObserver is null THEN
                RETURN
            END IF

            COMMENT: A broken observer must never take a live request down with it.
            COMMENT: This is host-supplied code running inside our transport callbacks;
            COMMENT: letting it throw would abort the request or response mid-flight.
            TRY
                CALL this.networkObserver PASSING direction, detail
            CATCH error
                COMMENT: Deliberately ignored
            END TRY

    END FUNCTION

    ====================
    PRIVATE METHODS
    ====================
    
    FUNCTION sendRequest(toExecute: NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Execute | array, 
                        openInBrowser: boolean, 
                        callback: function|null = null, thisArg: any = null)
        
        PURPOSE: The core network communication method. Handles all server communication.
        WHY: This method coordinates encryption, HTTPS requests, response parsing, and error handling.
        
        PARAMETERS:
            toExecute: One or more Execute objects wrapping components
            openInBrowser: If true, open in new window instead of making network request
            callback: Function called with (resultModel) when server replies
            thisArg: Context for the callback
        CALLBACK PARAMETERS:
            resultModel: (Required) NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Response - The response object returned from the server
        
        EXPLANATION:
            This method does several things:
            1. Wraps all components in a Request object
            2. Converts to JSON string
            3. Sends HTTPS POST to the gateway
            4. Receives response from server
            5. Parses JSON response
            6. Creates Response and Result objects
            7. Updates app state from results
            8. Calls callback with results
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: ==================== PREPARE THE REQUEST ====================
            COMMENT: Create a proper Request object using ObjectFactory
            CREATE requestModel AS ObjectFactory.CreateObject("Request", null, this)
            
            SET requestModel.core TO this
            SET requestModel.app_id TO this.appId
            SET requestModel.debug TO this.useDebugMode
            
            COMMENT: Add session ID if available
            IF this.appState is not null AND this.appState.session is not null AND this.appState.session.id is not null THEN
                SET requestModel.session_id TO this.appState.session.id
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Add components to the request using mixed-type handling
            IF toExecute is not null THEN
                COMMENT: Handle both single Execute object and array of Execute objects
                IF toExecute is array THEN
                    COMMENT: Array of Execute objects
                    IF toExecute.length > 0 THEN
                        CALL requestModel.setExecuteList(toExecute)
                    END IF
                ELSE
                    COMMENT: Single Execute object
                    CALL requestModel.setExecute(toExecute)
                END IF
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Convert the Request/Execute container models to gateway wire format.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: This is NOT requestModel.prepareForJson(). Building the payload is
            COMMENT: serialization, not model behavior, and the gateway's rules are not a
            COMMENT: straight property dump - see buildGatewayRequestObject() below. Request
            COMMENT: and Execute have NO prepareForJson() or importFromObject() overrides.
            CREATE plainObject AS CALL HttpRequestHelper.buildGatewayRequestObject(requestModel)
            COMMENT: Encode as JSON string for transmission
            CREATE requestString AS JSON_ENCODE(plainObject)
            
            COMMENT: ==================== SEND THE REQUEST ====================
            
            COMMENT: Loader components open external windows, not JSON API
            IF openInBrowser equals true THEN
                COMMENT: Create URL request with the same parameters as the background process
                CREATE browserRequest AS CREATE_URL_REQUEST(GATEWAY_URL)
                SET browserRequest.method TO "POST"
                SET browserRequest.contentType TO "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
                
                COMMENT: Add the request data as form parameter
                CREATE browserFormData AS "request=" + URL_ENCODE(requestString)
                SET browserRequest.data TO browserFormData
                
                COMMENT: Open in a new external window
                TRY
                    COMMENT: Determine window target from the component
                    CREATE browserTarget AS "_blank"
                    IF toExecute is not null AND toExecute is NOT array THEN
                        CREATE component AS toExecute.componentModel
                        IF component is not null AND component has property "browserTarget" AND component.browserTarget is not null THEN
                            SET browserTarget TO component.browserTarget
                        END IF
                    END IF

                    IF this.debugNetworkCalls equals true THEN
                        LOG_INFO("NETWORK: Opening external window to " + GATEWAY_URL + " with target " + browserTarget)
                        LOG_INFO("         Request Data: " + requestString)
                    END IF
                    CALL reportNetworkActivity("request", requestString)

                    OPEN_URL(browserRequest, browserTarget)

                CATCH error
                    IF this.debugNetworkCalls equals true THEN
                        LOG_ERROR("NETWORK: Error opening external window - " + error.message)
                    END IF
                    CALL reportNetworkActivity("error", "Error opening external window - " + error.message)
                END TRY
                
                COMMENT: Call callback with null (external windows don't return JSON responses)
                IF callback is not null THEN
                    CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING null
                END IF
                RETURN
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: ==================== MAKE THE HTTPS REQUEST ====================
            
            CREATE request AS CREATE_URL_REQUEST(GATEWAY_URL)
            SET request.method TO "POST"
            
            COMMENT: Set proper headers for JSON POST request
            SET request.contentType TO "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
            
            COMMENT: Send as form parameter "request" with the JSON string
            COMMENT: This is the format the Newgrounds API expects
            CREATE formData AS "request=" + URL_ENCODE(requestString)
            SET request.data TO formData
            
            COMMENT: Track the HTTP status separately from the outcome handlers.
            COMMENT: Many platforms report the status on its own event or property, which
            COMMENT: may fire BEFORE the success/error handler and is frequently absent
            COMMENT: entirely. Start it at UNKNOWN_STATUS and overwrite it if a real
            COMMENT: status ever arrives; never invent one.
            CREATE httpStatus AS UNKNOWN_STATUS

            CREATE onHttpStatus AS FUNCTION(event)
                SET httpStatus TO event.status
            END FUNCTION

            COMMENT: Set up event handlers
            CREATE onSuccess AS FUNCTION(event)
                IF this.debugNetworkCalls equals true THEN
                    LOG_INFO("NETWORK: Received response from server")
                    LOG_INFO("         Response Data: " + event.responseText)
                END IF
                CALL reportNetworkActivity("response", event.responseText)
                CALL onHTTPResponse(200, event.responseText, callback, thisArg)
            END FUNCTION
            
            CREATE onIOError AS FUNCTION(event)
                IF this.debugNetworkCalls equals true THEN
                    LOG_ERROR("NETWORK: IOError occurred - " + event.text)
                END IF
                CALL reportNetworkActivity("error", "IOError - " + event.text)

                COMMENT: Forward what the platform ACTUALLY reported, and UNKNOWN_STATUS
                COMMENT: (0) when it reported nothing. Do NOT substitute 500 here.
                COMMENT: See "no status is not a server error" under onHTTPResponse.
                COMMENT:
                COMMENT: If your platform exposes the status on a separate event that
                COMMENT: fires BEFORE this one, capture it there and read it here. If it
                COMMENT: exposes no status at all, pass UNKNOWN_STATUS every time - that
                COMMENT: is an honest answer, and 500 is not.
                CALL onHTTPResponse(httpStatus, null, callback, thisArg)
            END FUNCTION
            
            CREATE onSecurityError AS FUNCTION(event)
                IF this.debugNetworkCalls equals true THEN
                    LOG_ERROR("NETWORK: SecurityError occurred - " + event.text)
                END IF
                CALL reportNetworkActivity("error", "SecurityError - " + event.text)
                COMMENT: Security error occurred
                CALL onHTTPResponse(403, null, callback, thisArg)
            END FUNCTION
            
            COMMENT: Send the request
            TRY
                IF this.debugNetworkCalls equals true THEN
                    LOG_INFO("NETWORK: Sending request to " + GATEWAY_URL)
                    LOG_INFO("         Request Data: " + requestString)
                END IF
                CALL reportNetworkActivity("request", requestString)
                SEND_HTTP_REQUEST(request, onSuccess, onIOError, onSecurityError)
            CATCH error
                IF this.debugNetworkCalls equals true THEN
                    LOG_ERROR("NETWORK: Error sending request - " + error.message)
                END IF
                CALL reportNetworkActivity("error", "Error sending request - " + error.message)

                COMMENT: The send call threw, so the request never left the machine.
                COMMENT: There is no server to blame for a failure that happened here.
                CALL onHTTPResponse(UNKNOWN_STATUS, null, callback, thisArg)
            END TRY
        
    END FUNCTION
    
    FUNCTION onHTTPResponse(statusCode: integer, responseText: string|null, callback: function|null, thisArg: any = null)
        
        PURPOSE: Handle HTTP response from the server.
        WHY: Centralizes response processing, error handling, and callback management.
        
        PARAMETERS:
            statusCode: HTTP status code, or UNKNOWN_STATUS (0) when none was reported
            responseText: Response body from server
            callback: Developer's callback function
            thisArg: Context for the callback

        COMMENT: ---------------------------------------------------------------
        COMMENT: TURNING A STATUS INTO AN ERROR
        COMMENT: ---------------------------------------------------------------
        COMMENT:
        COMMENT: The Errors constants were chosen to mirror HTTP - 400, 403, 404, 429,
        COMMENT: 500, 503, 504 - so the common codes map straight across. Two cases need
        COMMENT: deciding: a status with no matching constant, and NO STATUS AT ALL.
        COMMENT:
        COMMENT: Map unrecognised codes BY CLASS, not to a generic error, so a 502 still
        COMMENT: reads as a server problem and a 418 still reads as a bad request:
        COMMENT:
        COMMENT:   400, 403, 404, 429, 500, 503, 504  the matching Errors constant
        COMMENT:   any other 5xx                      SERVER_ERROR
        COMMENT:   any other 4xx                      BAD_REQUEST
        COMMENT:   UNKNOWN_STATUS (0), or a 2xx here  INVALID_RESPONSE
        COMMENT:
        COMMENT: A MISSING STATUS IS NOT A SERVER ERROR. Many platforms report no status
        COMMENT: for a failed request - a Flash movie in a browser plugin almost never
        COMMENT: gets one - and substituting 500 maps it to SERVER_ERROR, whose message
        COMMENT: tells the player an unexpected error occurred on the server and to
        COMMENT: contact support. But no status usually means NO REPLY ARRIVED AT ALL:
        COMMENT: offline, DNS failure, a blocked domain, a request that never left the
        COMMENT: machine. Telling a player to contact support because their wifi dropped
        COMMENT: is worse than admitting you do not know.
        COMMENT:
        COMMENT: INVALID_RESPONSE (505) claims only what is actually known. Games
        COMMENT: branching on error.code will see 505 rather than 500 here, and that is
        COMMENT: the intended reading: 500 means THE SERVER SAID IT FAILED, 505 means NO
        COMMENT: USABLE REPLY WAS OBTAINED.
        COMMENT:
        COMMENT: A STATUS IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN, either. A 200 carrying an HTML error
        COMMENT: page, a proxy interstitial or a captive-portal login is a perfectly good
        COMMENT: HTTP response. Only inspecting the BODY catches those - which is why the
        COMMENT: decode below must be strict. See DECODING REQUIREMENTS.

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF this.debugNetworkCalls equals true THEN
                LOG_INFO("NETWORK: HTTP Response received with status " + statusCode)
                LOG_INFO("         Response Text: " + responseText)
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Create a Response object to hold all the results
            CREATE responseModel AS ObjectFactory.CreateObject("Response", null, this)

            COMMENT: Check HTTP status code
            COMMENT: 200-299 = success, anything else (including UNKNOWN_STATUS) = error
            IF statusCode < 200 OR statusCode > 299 THEN
                COMMENT: Map the status onto an Errors constant using the table above.
                COMMENT: Do NOT assume the status code IS an error code - most are not,
                COMMENT: and Errors.getError() handed an unmapped number produces a
                COMMENT: nameless error with no message.
                SET responseModel.error TO Errors.getError(
                    errorCodeForHttpStatus(statusCode),
                    describeHttpStatus(statusCode)
                )
            ELSE
                COMMENT: HTTP succeeded - parse the response JSON
                TRY
                    CREATE jsonObject AS JSON_DECODE(responseText)
                CATCH error
                    COMMENT: JSON parsing failed - create appropriate error
                    LOG_ERROR("JSON parsing error - " + error.message)

                    SET responseModel.error TO Errors.getError(
                        Errors.INVALID_RESPONSE,
                        "Unable to parse JSON response"
                    )

                    SET jsonObject TO null
                END TRY

                COMMENT: Import the JSON into the Response model.
                COMMENT:
                COMMENT: This is NOT responseModel.importFromObject(jsonObject). Turning a
                COMMENT: raw server response into a populated Response is a distinct job with
                COMMENT: a required order of operations - see importResponseObject() below.
                COMMENT: Two of its four steps cannot be expressed as an importFromObject
                COMMENT: override at all, which is why the whole job lives in a helper.
                IF jsonObject is not null THEN
                    TRY
                        CALL HttpResponseHelper.importResponseObject(responseModel, jsonObject)
                    CATCH importError
                        COMMENT: Importing JSON into model failed
                        LOG_ERROR("IMPORT ERROR: Error importing into Response model with object: "+ JSON_ENCODE(jsonObject)+ " :: " + importError.message)

                        SET responseModel.error TO Errors.getError(
                            Errors.INVALID_RESPONSE,
                            "Error importing response data"
                        )
                    END TRY
                END IF
            END IF
            
            COMMENT: Call the callback to return results to the developer
            IF callback is not null THEN
                CALL callback WITH context thisArg PASSING responseModel
            END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION buildRefusalResponse(component: NewgroundsIO.BaseComponent, preflightError): NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Response

        PURPOSE: Build the Response the gateway WOULD have returned, had it
        refused this component itself.
        WHY: So a locally-refused call reaches the caller through exactly the same
        path as a server-refused one. See the contract note in executeComponent.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE response AS ObjectFactory.CreateObject("Response", null, this)
            SET response.core TO this
            SET response.app_id TO this.appId

            COMMENT: ENVELOPE SUCCESS IS TRUE, and this is the important part.
            COMMENT: The REQUEST was fine - the component is what failed. That is
            COMMENT: exactly how the server reports "you are not logged in", and
            COMMENT: it puts the error at the layer callers already check.
            COMMENT: Reporting envelope failure instead would claim the whole
            COMMENT: batch was rejected, which is a different and worse claim.
            SET response.success TO true

            CALL response.setResult(buildRefusalResult(component, preflightError))

            RETURN response
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION buildRefusalResult(component: NewgroundsIO.BaseComponent, preflightError): NewgroundsIO.BaseResult

        PURPOSE: Build the single failed result for a refused component.

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: A component's objectName is "Component.method" - the same
            COMMENT: string the result factory keys on, split back into halves.
            CREATE splitAt AS the position of "." in component.objectName

            IF there is no "." in component.objectName THEN
                RETURN null
            END IF

            CREATE result AS ObjectFactory.CreateResult(
                the part of component.objectName before splitAt,
                the part of component.objectName after splitAt,
                null, this
            )

            COMMENT: An unrecognised component name yields null from the factory.
            IF result is null THEN
                RETURN null
            END IF

            SET result.core TO this
            SET result.success TO false
            SET result.error TO preflightError

            RETURN result
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION buildRefusalResponseList(refusedComponents: array): NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Response

        PURPOSE: Build a Response holding several refused components' results,
        for when EVERY component in a queue was refused and no request is sent.

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE response AS ObjectFactory.CreateObject("Response", null, this)
            SET response.core TO this
            SET response.app_id TO this.appId
            SET response.success TO true

            CREATE results AS new array
            FOR EACH refusal IN refusedComponents
                CREATE result AS buildRefusalResult(refusal.component, refusal.error)
                IF result is not null THEN
                    APPEND result TO results
                END IF
            END FOR

            CALL response.setResultList(results)

            RETURN response
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION mergeRefusalsIntoResponse(response, refusedComponents: array): NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Response

        PURPOSE: Add refused components' results to a response that DID come back
        from the server, so the caller sees one report covering everything it
        queued.

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF refusedComponents is empty THEN
                RETURN response
            END IF

            COMMENT: A transport failure means nothing came back to merge into.
            COMMENT: The refusals are still true, but reporting them on a response
            COMMENT: that does not exist would dress up a dead network as a
            COMMENT: partial success - so let the transport failure speak for
            COMMENT: itself.
            IF response is null THEN
                RETURN null
            END IF

            CREATE merged AS new array

            IF response.resultIsList() THEN
                APPEND every item in response.getResultList() TO merged
            ELSE IF response.getResult() is not null THEN
                APPEND response.getResult() TO merged
            END IF

            FOR EACH refusal IN refusedComponents
                CREATE result AS buildRefusalResult(refusal.component, refusal.error)
                IF result is not null THEN
                    APPEND result TO merged
                END IF
            END FOR

            COMMENT: ORDER IS NOT PRESERVED against the original queue - the
            COMMENT: server's results come first, then the refusals. Nothing reads
            COMMENT: results positionally (they are matched by component name),
            COMMENT: and promising an interleaving the two halves cannot actually
            COMMENT: guarantee would be worse than being plain about it.
            CALL response.setResultList(merged)

            RETURN response
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION errorCodeForHttpStatus(status: integer): integer

        PURPOSE: Map an HTTP status onto the closest Errors constant.
        WHY: So a failed load says "the server is down" or "that file is gone" rather
        than surfacing a raw platform error string the player cannot act on.

        BEHAVIOR:
            SWITCH status
                CASE 400: RETURN Errors.BAD_REQUEST
                CASE 403: RETURN Errors.USER_FORBIDDEN
                CASE 404: RETURN Errors.NOT_FOUND
                CASE 429: RETURN Errors.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS
                CASE 500: RETURN Errors.SERVER_ERROR
                CASE 503: RETURN Errors.SERVER_UNAVAILABLE
                CASE 504: RETURN Errors.GATEWAY_TIMEOUT
            END SWITCH

            COMMENT: Fall back BY CLASS rather than to a generic error.
            IF status is between 500 and 599 THEN
                RETURN Errors.SERVER_ERROR
            END IF

            IF status is between 400 and 499 THEN
                RETURN Errors.BAD_REQUEST
            END IF

            COMMENT: Covers UNKNOWN_STATUS (0) and any 2xx that reached here - the latter
            COMMENT: meaning the request succeeded and the BODY was the problem.
            RETURN Errors.INVALID_RESPONSE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION describeHttpStatus(status: integer): string

        PURPOSE: A sentence naming what failed and what the server said, if anything.
        WHY: The code tells a program what happened; this tells a person.

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF status equals UNKNOWN_STATUS THEN
                COMMENT: Not a fault - the platform simply did not hand us a code.
                RETURN "The request failed, and no HTTP status was reported"
            END IF

            IF status is between 200 and 299 THEN
                RETURN "The server returned HTTP " + status + " but the body was not valid JSON"
            END IF

            RETURN "The request failed with HTTP " + status
    END FUNCTION

END CLASS

COMMENT: ============================================================================
COMMENT: DECODING REQUIREMENTS
COMMENT: ============================================================================
COMMENT:
COMMENT: Your JSON decoder sits on both ends of this library, and two of its properties
COMMENT: are load-bearing. Both were real defects in a shipped library.
COMMENT:
COMMENT: 1. REJECT TRAILING CONTENT.
COMMENT:
COMMENT:    {"a":1}<html>...  must FAIL, not parse as {"a":1}.
COMMENT:
COMMENT:    A lenient scanner that stops at the end of the first value turns a
COMMENT:    captive-portal page, a proxy interstitial, or a server warning printed
COMMENT:    ahead of a real response into a plausible-looking success. A decoder that
COMMENT:    returns the NUMBER 0 for a page of HTML is the same bug wearing a more
COMMENT:    confusing hat: the leading '<' is garbage, but the scanner produced a value
COMMENT:    anyway. Parse a value, skip whitespace, and require end-of-input.
COMMENT:
COMMENT: 2. ACCEPT EXPONENT NOTATION, BECAUSE YOUR OWN ENCODER EMITS IT.
COMMENT:
COMMENT:    Any language whose number-to-string conversion switches to exponent form for
COMMENT:    very small or very large values will write 1e-7 into a cloud save. If the
COMMENT:    decoder's number scanner does not handle 'e'/'E' with an optional sign, THE
COMMENT:    LIBRARY CANNOT READ BACK WHAT IT JUST WROTE - and the failure only shows up
COMMENT:    on the player's next launch, in data that is already saved.
COMMENT:
COMMENT:    Do not assume: round-trip the extremes of your platform's number range
COMMENT:    through encode -> decode and compare. This one went unnoticed for years
COMMENT:    because the encoder and decoder were only ever tested apart.


COMMENT: ============================================================================
COMMENT: SERIALIZATION HELPERS
COMMENT: ============================================================================
COMMENT:
COMMENT: These two procedures are the request and response halves of gateway
COMMENT: serialization. They are shown here as static helpers because that is where
COMMENT: they belong: they are transport concerns, not model behavior.
COMMENT:
COMMENT: Put them wherever your language makes static helpers natural - a separate
COMMENT: file, a module, private methods on Core. What matters is that they are NOT
COMMENT: prepareForJson()/importFromObject() overrides on Request, Execute or Response.
COMMENT: Those three models have no serialization overrides at all.
COMMENT:
COMMENT: The reference libraries name them HttpRequestHelper.buildGatewayRequestObject()
COMMENT: and HttpResponseHelper.importResponseObject().

CLASS HttpRequestHelper

    FUNCTION buildGatewayRequestObject(requestModel: NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Request): object

        PURPOSE: Convert a Request model into the plain object the gateway expects.
        WHY: The gateway distinguishes an ABSENT key from a key holding null or false,
        so the payload is not a dump of the model's properties.

        RETURNS: A plain object ready to be JSON encoded

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE requestObject AS new empty object

            COMMENT: === Field inclusion rules ===
            COMMENT: app_id      always
            COMMENT: session_id  only when not null
            COMMENT: debug       ONLY WHEN TRUE - omit entirely when false
            COMMENT: echo        only when not null
            COMMENT: execute     always; single object or array, matching what was attached

            SET requestObject.app_id TO requestModel.app_id

            IF requestModel.session_id is not null THEN
                SET requestObject.session_id TO requestModel.session_id
            END IF

            COMMENT: Note the test is "equals true", not "is not null". Sending
            COMMENT: debug:false is NOT the same as omitting the key - a debug-flagged
            COMMENT: request is validated differently by the server, so emitting it
            COMMENT: unconditionally changes behavior for every release build. This is
            COMMENT: invisible from the client: nothing errors and the request succeeds.
            IF requestModel.debug equals true THEN
                SET requestObject.debug TO true
            END IF

            IF requestModel.echo is not null THEN
                SET requestObject.echo TO requestModel.echo
            END IF

            COMMENT: === Attach the execute payload ===
            COMMENT: Request holds EITHER execute OR executeList, never both - the
            COMMENT: setters clear each other. Serialize whichever one is set.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: NOTE THE NAME: this is executeIsArray(), while the matching test on
            COMMENT: Response is resultIsList(). The two genuinely differ. Match them
            COMMENT: rather than regularizing - shared code that probes for one by name
            COMMENT: will miss the other.
            IF CALL requestModel.executeIsArray() THEN
                CREATE executeList AS new array
                FOR EACH executeModel IN CALL requestModel.getExecuteList()
                    APPEND CALL buildExecuteObject(executeModel) TO executeList
                END FOR
                SET requestObject.execute TO executeList
            ELSE IF CALL requestModel.getExecute() is not null THEN
                SET requestObject.execute TO CALL buildExecuteObject(CALL requestModel.getExecute())
            ELSE
                SET requestObject.execute TO null
            END IF

            RETURN requestObject
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION buildExecuteObject(executeModel: NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Execute): object

        PURPOSE: Convert one Execute wrapper into wire format, encrypting if required.
        WHY: Encryption applies to the whole execute object, not to individual fields,
        and it happens at serialization time - not when the component was created.

        RETURNS: Either a plain execute object, or { secure: "<encrypted string>" }

        BEHAVIOR:
            CREATE componentModel AS executeModel.componentModel

            COMMENT: Build the plain form first. Both fields were already populated by
            COMMENT: Execute.setComponent(): `component` is the full dotted path
            COMMENT: ("Medal.unlock") taken from componentModel.objectName, and
            COMMENT: `parameters` is the component's own serialized output - its
            COMMENT: propertyNames only, never the transport flags.
            CREATE plainExecute AS new empty object
            SET plainExecute.component TO executeModel.component
            SET plainExecute.parameters TO executeModel.parameters

            COMMENT: Secure components get the ENTIRE execute object encrypted and
            COMMENT: wrapped, so the component name and its parameters are both hidden.
            COMMENT: Encrypt at this point - not earlier - because the plain object has
            COMMENT: to be fully built before it can be serialized and enciphered.
            IF componentModel is not null AND componentModel.isSecure equals true THEN
                IF executeModel.core is null THEN
                    THROW error "Core is required for encrypting secure components."
                END IF

                CREATE encryptedString AS CALL executeModel.core.encryptObject(plainExecute)

                COMMENT: The encrypted form carries ONLY `secure` - no component name,
                COMMENT: no parameters. That is the whole point of the wrapper.
                CREATE secureExecute AS new empty object
                SET secureExecute.secure TO encryptedString
                RETURN secureExecute
            END IF

            RETURN plainExecute
    END FUNCTION

END CLASS


CLASS HttpResponseHelper

    FUNCTION importResponseObject(responseModel: NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Response, jsonObject: object)

        PURPOSE: Populate a Response model from the gateway's decoded reply.
        WHY: This is more than one importFromObject() call, and THE ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING.

        COMMENT: Why this cannot be an importFromObject() override on Response:
        COMMENT: step 1 has to happen BEFORE the base import runs, and step 4 has to
        COMMENT: happen AFTER it. An override only gives you one place to stand.

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: ===== STEP 1: Take `result` out BEFORE the base import =====
            COMMENT: The base import walks declared properties and casts them by type.
            COMMENT: Handed a raw result payload it has no cast type for, it will try to
            COMMENT: cast data it cannot type. Remove it first, deal with it separately.
            CREATE rawResult AS null
            IF jsonObject has key "result" THEN
                SET rawResult TO jsonObject.result
                REMOVE key "result" FROM jsonObject
            END IF

            COMMENT: ===== STEP 2: Run the base import =====
            COMMENT: This populates the Response's own properties: success, error,
            COMMENT: app_id, debug, api_version and so on - and casts `error` into a
            COMMENT: real Error model, which step 4 depends on.
            CALL responseModel.importFromObject(jsonObject)

            COMMENT: ===== STEP 3: Build the typed result models =====
            COMMENT: The gateway returns either one result object or an array of them,
            COMMENT: mirroring whether the request carried one execute or a list.
            IF rawResult is not null THEN

                IF rawResult is array THEN
                    CREATE resultList AS new array
                    FOR EACH rawEntry IN rawResult
                        CREATE resultModel AS CALL buildResultModel(rawEntry, responseModel.core)
                        COMMENT: An unrecognized component name yields null from the
                        COMMENT: factory. Skip that entry rather than failing the whole
                        COMMENT: response - a gateway that gained a component your build
                        COMMENT: predates should not break every other result in the batch.
                        IF resultModel is not null THEN
                            APPEND resultModel TO resultList
                        END IF
                    END FOR
                    CALL responseModel.setResultList(resultList)
                ELSE
                    CREATE resultModel AS CALL buildResultModel(rawResult, responseModel.core)
                    IF resultModel is not null THEN
                        CALL responseModel.setResult(resultModel)
                    END IF
                END IF
            END IF

            COMMENT: ===== STEP 4: Propagate a response-level error down =====
            COMMENT: MUST run after step 2, so what gets copied is the TYPED Error model
            COMMENT: built by the base import - not the raw dictionary it was decoded from.
            COMMENT:
            COMMENT: Why this exists: a transport-level failure produces an error on the
            COMMENT: response and results with empty error slots. Callers check the RESULT
            COMMENT: - that is where component outcomes live - so without this they see no
            COMMENT: error at all and treat the call as having quietly returned nothing.
            IF responseModel.error is not null THEN
                FOR EACH resultModel IN CALL getAllResults(responseModel)
                    IF resultModel.error is null THEN
                        SET resultModel.error TO responseModel.error
                    END IF
                END FOR
            END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION buildResultModel(rawEntry: object, core: NewgroundsIO.Core): NewgroundsIO.BaseResult | null

        PURPOSE: Turn one raw result entry into its typed result model.
        WHY: Results are typed per component, so the component name selects the class.

        RETURNS: The populated result model, or null if the component is unrecognized

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: A usable entry names its component and carries a data payload.
            COMMENT: Anything else is not something this build knows how to type.
            IF rawEntry is null OR rawEntry has no key "component" OR rawEntry has no key "data" THEN
                RETURN null
            END IF

            COMMENT: The entry names its own component as a dotted path, e.g. "Medal.unlock"
            CREATE componentPath AS rawEntry.component

            COMMENT: Split on the dot - the factory takes scope and method separately.
            COMMENT: Reject a path with no dot, or with nothing on either side of it,
            COMMENT: rather than handing the factory an empty scope or method name.
            CREATE dotPosition AS the index of the first "." in componentPath
            IF dotPosition is not found
               OR dotPosition equals 0
               OR dotPosition equals (componentPath.length - 1) THEN
                RETURN null
            END IF

            CREATE componentScope AS componentPath from 0 up to dotPosition
            CREATE componentMethod AS componentPath from (dotPosition + 1) to the end

            CREATE resultModel AS ObjectFactory.CreateResult(
                componentScope, componentMethod, rawEntry.data, core
            )
            IF resultModel is null THEN
                RETURN null
            END IF

            COMMENT: Feed the cache. THIS is the "automatic updates" mechanism - state
            COMMENT: refreshes because the response helper pushes every typed result
            COMMENT: through here, not because any model overrides importFromObject.
            COMMENT: Skip it and cached medals, scoreboards and save slots silently
            COMMENT: never refresh: every call succeeds, every cached value goes stale.
            IF core is not null AND core.appState is not null THEN
                CALL core.appState.setValueFromResult(resultModel)
            END IF

            RETURN resultModel
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION getAllResults(responseModel: NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Response): array

        PURPOSE: Return every result on a response as a flat list, however it is stored.
        WHY: Step 4 has to walk them all, and Response holds either one or a list.

        BEHAVIOR:
            IF CALL responseModel.resultIsList() THEN
                CREATE resultList AS CALL responseModel.getResultList()
                IF resultList is null THEN
                    RETURN new empty array
                END IF
                RETURN resultList
            END IF

            CREATE singleResult AS CALL responseModel.getResult()
            IF singleResult is null THEN
                RETURN new empty array
            END IF
            RETURN [singleResult]
    END FUNCTION

END CLASS
